# remote-tailnet-guard - repository hygiene / ignore rules
#
# LAST UPDATED  : 2026-09-24 (task t39 - tools/ listed in the release set so the uninstaller
#                 ships with a clone; task t12 completed the internal-material list)
# COMMANDS USED : powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File
#                 .github/scripts/repo-hygiene.ps1        (reads this file to prove the
#                 internal material below is excluded)
#
# NOTE: the gate script holds the blocked-identifier patterns, so this file refers to them
# by name instead of quoting them - quoting them here would make the release-set scan
# report this file. See .github/scripts/repo-hygiene.ps1 section 0 for the actual list.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. INTERNAL MATERIAL - deliberately NOT part of the released repository
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The release set is exactly:
#   src/  i18n/  tests/  panel/  tools/  docs/collect.md  docs/install/
#   docs/threat-model.md  SECURITY.md  LICENSE  README.md  CHANGELOG.md
#   CONTRIBUTING.md  .gitignore  .editorconfig  .github/**
# Everything else under docs/ is internal analysis and review material: it contains
# machine specifics gathered while the checks were designed, so it is excluded on purpose.
# README.md states the same thing for readers ("Internal analysis and review material does
# not ship with the repository"), and repo-hygiene.ps1 fails if a file listed here is
# missing from this section.
docs/baseline.md
docs/matrix.md
docs/harness-contract.md
docs/defensive-spec.md
docs/security-review.md
docs/security-review-r2.md
docs/security-review-r3.md
docs/verify-t7.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Collector / prerequisite-checker output (opt-in report files only)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# collect.ps1 writes ZERO bytes unless the caller passes -OutFile / -DumpFixture, and
# panel/prereq.ps1 has no output-file switch at all. Anything either can produce is a local
# report and must never be committed (it may contain live peer addresses).
*.report.json
*-report.json
rtg-report*
out/
*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Binary products - this repository is text-only
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.exe
*.dll
*.msi
*.msix
*.zip
*.7z
*.cab
*.pdb
*.nupkg

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Secret stores and credential material (defence in depth)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The plugin never reads, prints, stores or transmits these; this section exists so that an
# accidental copy never gets committed. See SECURITY.md promise P4.
.credentials.yaml
*.credentials.yaml
*.token
*.pem
*.pfx
*.key
ext-bridge-token*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. OS / editor litter
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.swp
*~
.vscode/
.idea/
